 that must be what we're looking for  amazing is there reflected back on my  own travel experiences I realized that  the majority of my trips were amazing  but some were better than others some  were more impactful and I couldn't put  my finger on what that was no textbook  on the tourism industry would be  complete without a chapter on Abraham  Maslow psychologists who studied  motivation in humans he created the  hierarchy of needs to say that people  inherently seek self-actualization when  they feel like they're reaching their  full potential and along the way they  must meet certain needs and when they do  they're more likely to have what he  calls peak experiences he defines these  as moments of the highest happiness  where people feel like they've found  their place in the world I sent these  definitions off to the student body of  the GSB and I asked them have you ever  had any peak experiences the answers  work great this is just a snippet one of  them was from someone who served in  Afghanistan as a pilot and after a  particularly challenging mission he said  he literally felt a calming state of  Nirvana this was impactful because of  all of the responses I got his was the  only one that described a time when he  was at work and he was serving our  country in Afghanistan  these are the moments that make life  worth living for when you feel so much  joy and love and you feel like you found  your place in this world this is exactly  what I was looking for that defines the  amazing trips and the transformational  trips if we can't find these peak  experiences when we're at work when will  we when will you getting the most out of  your vacation takes a lot of practice  and a little bit of knowledge and to  help you with that I created a framework  gabby's hierarchy of vacation and at the  base at the minimum you need to  disconnect and take your vacation days  next you need to understand that too  many expectations are setting you up for  disaster because things will go wrong  and when they do you want to try and  find a little bit of pleasure in them  but when the things go right you want to  make sure that those are the memorable  experiences and you remember them and  when you do you'll be set up for peak  experiences my trips have taken me all  over the world and so much has gone  wrong I have lost dozens of passports  literally and yes I've been  strip-searched in Israel but I have also  had those rare moments of joy and  happiness where I have felt in Wonder  and awe of the world my hope for you is  that you have on-time departures and  toilets that you're familiar with  and that you have many many peak  experiences along the way I hope you  enjoy your vacation thank you
 

